{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dispiteous-balsamic-isopod","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n`tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` (1,890 LOC, 37 top-level test functions on origin/main, not 32) was written to grep two hand-copied gate lists; its own docstring records that the lists are now ONE reusable workflow, so 11 of its tests re-assert `.github/workflows/*.yml` config snapshots and duplicate `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` (184 LOC) and `tests/unit/test_gerrit_docs_only.py:31-53`. `tests/unit/test_verify_gate_parity.py::test_real_repo_verify_gate_is_in_parity` (`:115`) re-runs that script in-process while the script runs only as a CI step (`_build-and-test.yml:145-152`), not from `make lint`. The per-test verdicts (table (4)) are itemised in this ticket's first comment. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\nPer table (4):\n- Delete tests 2 `test_matrix_keeps_every_test_tier_but_collects_coverage_once`, 3 `test_diff_coverage_step…`, 4 `test_scanner_gate_uses_one_reusable…`, 5 `test_mutation_gate_uses_one_reusable…`, 6 `test_mutation_workflows_are_bounded_and_publish_results`, 9 `test_mutation_reusable_expands_selector_json…` (`:463-766`), 10 `test_shared_gate_signatures_live_in_the_reusable`, 11 `test_documentation_gate_signatures_live_in_the_shared_action`, 20 `test_repo_policy_nodes_partition_the_default_selection_exactly` (`:1208`; it hard-codes node ids that S3 and S4 delete, which is why this story lands before them), 35 `test_makefile_lint_runs_both_config_gates`, 36 `test_ci_runs_the_config_gates_through_make_lint_not_a_duplicate_step` (wiring moves to the S3 census).\n- Rewrite 19 `test_optionality_contract_gates_the_verified_path` (`:1086`) to parametrize over every `uses: ./.github/workflows/_*.yml` job in `gerrit-verify.yaml` (6 jobs, `:220-308`), asserting `with.gerrit-refspec == \"${{ inputs.GERRIT_REFSPEC }}\"` and that a push/PR lane `uses` the same reusable; this subsumes 4 and 5.\n- Keep 21 `test_repo_policy_nodes_run_only_in_the_existing_primary_cell` (`:1221`) minus the job-set snapshot at `:1231`; keep every other test the table marks KEEP.\n- Remove the helpers and constants left unused: `_SHARED_GATE_SIGNATURES`, `_DOCUMENTATION_GATE_SIGNATURES`, `_COVERAGE_FLAGS`, `_expanded_test_matrix`, `_coverage_flags_by_cell`, `_REPO_POLICY_MODULES`, `_REPO_POLICY_NODE_IDS`.\n- Net for the module: 37 → 26 top-level functions (25 kept unchanged in name + the rewritten 19); the 11 named deletions are the whole delete set.\n- Survivor between `tests/unit/test_verify_gate_parity.py` and the script: the script. Delete `test_real_repo_verify_gate_is_in_parity` (`:115`); keep the 7 synthetic tests (`:53-109`), which hold the RED half of the script's contract. Add `python scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` after `Makefile:439` with a two-line `@#` comment naming this story. The CI step stays; the ~50 ms double run is accepted because workflow files are out of this epic's scope. The script's remaining assertion (`scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py:143-165`): `vote.needs` ⊇ every job of `test.yml`/`optionality.yml`/`verify-identity.yml`/`prompt-eval.yml` minus `EXCLUDED_JOBS`, plus `classify`/`docs-only`.\n- `_OPTIONALITY_SUITE_ITEM_COUNT` (`:1132`) stays at 10 in this story; S4 sets it to 9 when it deletes one `test_core_optionality.py` test.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`, `tests/unit/test_verify_gate_parity.py`, `Makefile`. Out of scope: every file under `.github/workflows/`, `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` itself, `tests/unit/test_gerrit_docs_only.py`, and the check-script twins (S3).\n\n## Testing\n`pytest --collect-only -q tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py tests/unit/test_verify_gate_parity.py` before and after: exactly 12 fewer top-level test functions (11 + 1) plus the delta from parametrizing 19 over the 6 jobs; both collect counts are recorded on this ticket. `make lint` runs the parity script and prints `Verified-gate parity: OK`; `make test` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The 25 kept functions plus the rewritten 19 collect from `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`; each of the 11 deleted names collects nothing (`pytest --collect-only -q tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py -k <name>` per name).\n- [ ] `make lint` invokes `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` (verified by `make -n lint | grep check_verify_gate_parity`).\n- [ ] The RED half of the script's contract still holds on synthetic input via the 7 kept tests in `tests/unit/test_verify_gate_parity.py` (`pytest tests/unit/test_verify_gate_parity.py` green, 7 nodes).\n- [ ] `_SHARED_GATE_SIGNATURES`, `_DOCUMENTATION_GATE_SIGNATURES`, `_COVERAGE_FLAGS`, `_expanded_test_matrix`, `_coverage_flags_by_cell`, `_REPO_POLICY_MODULES`, `_REPO_POLICY_NODE_IDS` are gone (`git grep -n` on each name under `tests/` prints nothing).\n- [ ] `make verify` green.","id":"bbce-1846-1dd1-49ca","parent_id":"f400-65b3-1899-4af9","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Collapse the CI-parity guards and run check_verify_gate_parity from make lint"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788807150223343600,"uuid":"75bfe48d-28e5-4844-9b21-7b45c0f4ff86"}